# SlugBase i18n — Tolgee-first Rule (spec §17)

## Policy

SlugBase ships **English (en) and German (de)** at v1. Every string surfaced in the UI — labels, errors, toasts, tooltips, empty-state copy, confirmation dialogs, accessible `aria-label`s — **must be in the message catalog**. Hard-coded strings in component/template code are a commit-blocker.

## Authoritative tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Tolgee** | Translation-management **mirror** synced from repo catalogs. **Self-hosted `https://tolgee.mdg-labs.dev`; project `4` (`/projects/4`)** |
| `TOLGEE_API_KEY` | Infisical key (Tolgee PAT) — never hard-code, never log |
| `TOLGEE_PROJECT_ID` | `4` — identifies the SlugBase project in the Tolgee instance |

**Repo source of truth:** typed catalogs in `packages/web/app/i18n/messages.ts` and `packages/marketing/src/i18n/messages.ts` (en **and** de together). Tolgee CLI reads/writes **JSON** at `.tolgee/export/{languageTag}.json` (generated, not hand-edited). Astro marketing is **not** parsed by Tolgee CLI — sync is JSON push/pull only.

The **Tolgee React SDK** loads `staticData` from those TS catalogs at runtime (**React Router v7** web app). Marketing uses the same keys via `t(locale, key)` at build time. Optional DevTools when `VITE_TOLGEE_API_URL` / `PUBLIC_TOLGEE_API_URL` is set.

## Tolgee CLI workflow (export → push → CI diff)

```bash
# 1. Edit messages.ts (web + marketing) — add en AND de for every new key
pnpm i18n:export                    # messages.ts → .tolgee/export/en.json + de.json
infisical run --env=dev -- pnpm i18n:push   # upload to Tolgee project 4

# 2. CI / pre-commit gate
pnpm i18n:check:tolgee              # export + pull + strict repo↔Tolgee diff
pnpm i18n:check:hardcoded           # no inline UI strings in tsx/astro
```

- **`i18n:compare:web`** (optional): `tolgee compare` on web TSX only — never include `*.astro`.
- After adding keys locally, run **`i18n:push`** before merge or CI will fail (repo ahead of Tolgee).

## Authoring rule — new UI code

1. **Author against the catalog**: write `t('key.name')` (or the framework equivalent) — never inline English strings.
2. **Add the key to both locale blocks** in the relevant `messages.ts`, then **`pnpm i18n:push`** to sync Tolgee.
3. **German translation required before merge**: a missing German string is a Fast-Follow blocker, not an acceptable v1 gap. Either add the translation or create a SB Jira task with label `i18n` before merging.
4. **Key naming convention**: `<scope>.<context>.<descriptor>` — all lowercase, dots as separators, no abbreviations.
   - ✅ `bookmark.list.empty_state_title`
   - ✅ `auth.login.password_placeholder`
   - ❌ `bkmrk_lst_empty` (abbreviations)
   - ❌ `BookmarkList.emptyState.title` (camelCase / PascalCase)
5. **No JSX-only translation workarounds**: translation functions only, not inline HTML or separate `<Trans>` strings that circumvent the catalog.

## Language resolution order (spec §17)

```
signed-in user preference → Accept-Language → fallback: en
```

The user preference is stored as a `language` column on the `user_account` entity (spec §16). The server sets the locale on every response; the client does not make a separate language-resolution request.

## AI suggestion output language (spec §17)

When invoking the AI-suggest feature, pass the user's resolved locale as the `outputLanguage` hint. The suggestion cache key includes `output_language` (spec §16 — AI suggestion cache). Do not default to English when the user preference is set to German.

## Infisical secrets for Tolgee

| Key | `.env.example` placeholder | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `TOLGEE_API_KEY` | `TOLGEE_API_KEY=` | Tolgee Personal Access Token (server-side SDK calls and CLI) — secret, value only in Infisical |
| `TOLGEE_PROJECT_ID` | `TOLGEE_PROJECT_ID=4` | SlugBase project in the Tolgee instance (`https://tolgee.mdg-labs.dev/projects/4`) |
| `VITE_TOLGEE_API_URL` | `VITE_TOLGEE_API_URL=https://tolgee.mdg-labs.dev` | Web client (Vite); optional DevTools |
| `PUBLIC_TOLGEE_API_URL` | `PUBLIC_TOLGEE_API_URL=https://tolgee.mdg-labs.dev` | Marketing (Astro); optional DevTools |

Register all three via `infisical secrets set ... --env=dev` and add the `.env.example` stubs before writing any Tolgee-consuming code.

## Verifier checks (Layer 3c)

For any task that adds or changes UI strings, verify:

```bash
# No hard-coded user-visible strings in new/changed component files
rg -n '"[A-Z][a-z]' packages/web/src

# Keys follow naming convention (no camelCase separators)
rg -n 't\("[a-z][a-zA-Z]' packages/web/src

# Tolgee env vars are in .env.example
rg -n "^TOLGEE_" .env.example
```

## Forbidden

- **Inline English strings in UI code** — `<p>No bookmarks yet</p>` — use `t('bookmark.list.empty_state_title')`.
- **Skipping German on merge** — create the Jira `i18n` task first.
- **Hard-coding `TOLGEE_API_KEY` anywhere** — it must come from Infisical.
- **Silently falling back to key name** — log a warning in development when a key is missing; throw in CI if the default locale has unmapped keys.
